IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 3533 of 2023
CITATION: 2023 SCC OnLine SC 877
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: J.K. Maheshwari, K.V. Viswanathan

PARTIES:
Universal Sompo vs Suresh Chand Jain

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Consumer Protection Act, 2019

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 58 Consumer Protection, Section 67 Consumer Protection

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
ncdrc orders appeal, writ jurisdiction against ncdrc, remedy exhaustion

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Clarified appellate hierarchy under the Consumer Protection Act 2019, discouraging High Courts from entertaining Article 226 petitions against NCDRC orders when statutory appeals exist.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 58 Consumer Protection, Section 67 Consumer Protection.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

